# The model, and optionally the effort, each agent role runs on: `role model [effort]`.
# Mestari reads this file from main, never from the branch under review.
# Roles: build (first build round), fix (later build rounds), review (first full review),
# re-review (normal-risk fix-only review), review-2 (second high-risk reviewer), triage
# (`paja triage`), plan (the pool's planner) and init (`paja init`'s detection of the project's
# stacks, checks and environment). A line naming another role is skipped, and `paja doctor` warns
# about it.
# A `fallback <model>` line names a model to use when the chosen one is busy.
# A role with no line runs on the account's default model.
build sonnet
fix sonnet
review opus
re-review sonnet medium
review-2 sonnet medium
# triage (the follow-up sorting pass of `paja triage`) is the cheapest model.
triage haiku
# plan (the pool's planner, listing the files an item will touch) is cheap too.
plan haiku
# init (`paja init`'s agent, which reads a repository to find its stacks and checks) needs a
# capable model; with no line it runs on the account's default.
init sonnet
# The most turns one session of a role may take: `max-turns <role> <turns>`. A role with no
# line gets 80 (build, fix) or 30 (the reviews); no session runs uncapped.
max-turns build 80
max-turns fix 80
max-turns review 30
max-turns re-review 30
max-turns review-2 30
max-turns plan 15
